+# T-44446: T331/T332 router dependency map
+
+## Observed facts
+
+- `backend/app/main.py` is still 857 lines. It creates the app via `create_application`, owns lifespan setup, and wires most routes in the module body.
+- Runtime-backed globals remain: `mongo_client`, `telemetry_collection` (main.py:168-169), `bus` and `simulations` (568-570), plus `bearer`, auth dependency aliases, and admin-role aliases (166, 242-279). Lifespan creates `RuntimeState` and writes `application.state.runtime` (172-225). The packet states typed `RuntimeState`, `get_runtime`, `get_pool`, `get_database`, and `current_user` providers are already implemented.
+- Direct module routers already included: membership (`membership_router`), pit reads (`pit_router`), analytics (`analytics_router`). Main imports these router objects (main.py:102-106, 326, 400, 749); membership/analytics/pit reads are adopted per packet interface.
+- Remaining factories wired in main: CRUD (`create_crud_router` through `crud_routes` and `register_resources`, main.py:295-324); auth; user; session action; results read/write; stewards; pit writes; telemetry; pit strategy; demo races; live websocket; legacy/readiness health; DBMS SQL/Mongo; race archive; laps; DBMS lock. `create_application` is also still main's app/lifespan factory. Most have handler aliases retained in main for compatibility.
+- Notable direct captures: `create_auth_router(... current_user ...)`; `create_pit_strategy_router(... load_pit_strategy_rows, load_pit_telemetry, ..., jsonable)`; `create_demo_race_router(... connection, dict_row, mongo_ready, ...)`; DBMS/archive/laps factories receive some direct function objects and other late-looking lambdas. Factory-local `Depends` values are formed during router construction. These bindings do not follow later replacement of a main attribute unless the passed callable itself resolves the main global at call time.
+- Router-specific surfaces: auth factory accepts origin check, fetch getter, serializer, secure-cookie getter and current-user callable (`auth_router.py:39-46`); demo-race factory accepts 13 positional collaborators and has internal route closures (`demo_race_router.py:64-79`); pit-strategy factory accepts 9 collaborators and returns a handler alias (`pit_strategy_router.py:16-27`). CRUD requires 15 explicit collaborator arguments (`api/crud.py:11-31`). These are real API implementation contracts; preserve paths, methods, shapes, and behavior.
+- `backend/tests/test_auth_runtime.py` is absent. `backend/tests/test_api.py` contains the auth/cookie, pit-strategy, demo-race, DBMS, and lifespan cases listed below; no credential values were read.
+
+## Test bindings and blockers
+
+- `test_api.py` patches `main_module.fetch_one`, `fetch_all`, `mongo_ready`, `connection`, `publish`, `cancel_automatic_pit_reservations`, `APP_ENV`, `acquire_runtime_lease`, `check_runtime_lease`, `get_pool`, `open_pool`, `close_pool`, `MongoClient`, `resume_or_create_auto_demo_race`, and `mongo_database_ready`. Several endpoints/factory registrations receive collaborators directly, so patches made after app import will not replace those captured objects. Keep these patch points as dynamic provider lookups until each test migrates to app dependency overrides.
+- Direct legacy handler reads include `main_module.admin`, `decide_incident`, `control_simulation`, `constraint_demo`, `simulations`, `fetch_one`, `dbms_mongo_collections`, `dbms_mongo_collection_documents`, `record_simulated_incidents`, `delete_demo_race`, plus `Decision`, `SimulationControl`, and `SimulationControl`-related model symbols. Removing compatibility aliases before updating these tests would break test bindings even if HTTP routes still work.
+- Strongest closure-capture blockers by named test: `test_pit_strategy_reports_pending_live_decision_and_historical_stops` patches fetch functions and reads `simulations`; `test_dbms_mongo_collection_browser_lists_real_collections_and_pages_filtered_documents` patches `mongo_database_ready` but reads handler aliases; `test_demo_delete_waits_for_simulator_and_validates_before_stopping` patches `connection`/`mongo_ready` and reads `simulations`/`delete_demo_race`; `test_app_lifespan_starts_resources_and_awaits_simulator_shutdown` patches pool, Mongo, lease and resume functions and reads runtime globals. `test_cookie_auth_login_sets_secure_cookies_outside_local_mode` patches `APP_ENV`; `test_simulation_stop_clears_pending_pit_reservations` patches `mongo_ready` and cancellation and reads `control_simulation`.
+- Other tests patch `connection`/`publish` for reservation/results/incident handlers or `fetch_one` for results; keep those functions late-bound or replace these bindings with explicit FastAPI dependency overrides in the same step. Existing `main` identity monkeypatches are the concrete reason aliases cannot all disappear in one change.
+
+## Proposed next six atomic packets
+
+Packets have one worker and role-correct files. W3 test characterization precedes the matching W2 adoption; the temporary factory tests use fakes and preserve all current API assertions. Line counts are estimates (added plus deleted), each intended to stay below 150; validate scope and actual diff when each packet is written. Offline verify for each packet: `env APP_ENV=local PYTHONPATH=backend .venv/bin/pytest -q backend/tests/test_contract_snapshot.py backend/tests/test_request_dependencies.py backend/tests/test_runtime_dependencies.py && .venv/bin/ruff check backend/app backend/tests`. Root gate after each accepted packet: `bash scripts/eval/db-baseline.sh`. Proposed checks were not run for this audit.
+
+1. **W3 — Demo delete fixture preparation**. Target only `backend/tests/test_api.py`. Refactor the delete-ordering test setup into test-local fake collaborators and exercise `run_demo_race_delete` directly; retain the existing HTTP contract tests and assertions. Estimate: ≤55 changed lines. Offline verify: use the shared offline command above; the new fake/direct characterization should be run only after implementation confirms it avoids database fixtures.
+2. **W2 — Demo route database providers**. Target only `backend/app/demo_race_router.py` and `backend/app/main.py`. Replace the route's captured connection and Mongo getter with existing runtime-backed Depends providers; keep the other service callbacks and public route contracts. Do not replace the full 13-argument factory in this packet. Estimate: ≤120 changed lines. Offline verify: use the shared offline command above; do not select the existing generated-demo API tests because they use database fixtures.
+3. **W3 — Demo route override coverage**. Target only `backend/tests/test_api.py`. Move the HTTP delete test's DB and Mongo setup to FastAPI dependency overrides; keep simulation/deletion ordering assertions. Estimate: ≤65 changed lines. Offline verify: use the shared offline command above; validate any focused test selection against its fixtures before adding it.
+4. **W3 — Pit strategy factory characterization**. Target only `backend/tests/test_api.py`. Add direct router-factory coverage with fake strategy rows, telemetry, simulation, and serializer providers before changing main registration; retain existing projection and wire-shape assertions. Estimate: ≤70 changed lines. Offline verify: use the shared offline command above; add a focused selection only after confirming it uses fakes and no database fixture.
+5. **W2 — Pit strategy runtime providers**. Target only `backend/app/pit_strategy_router.py` and `backend/app/main.py`. Resolve runtime simulation, database reads, and Mongo collection through Depends-backed runtime providers, preserving projection and the main compatibility alias until W3 removes its reads. Do not change service logic. Estimate: ≤120 changed lines. Offline verify: use the shared offline command above; the existing pit-strategy API case is excluded because it uses a database fixture.
+6. **W3 — Auth current-user override coverage**. Target only `backend/tests/test_api.py`. Convert the current-user route case to `app.dependency_overrides` and verify cleanup; then a separate W2 packet can adopt runtime fetch/config providers in `auth_router.py` and `main.py`. Estimate: ≤45 changed lines. Offline verify: use the shared offline command above; confirm any focused selection is fake-only before adding it.
+
+## Boundaries and risks
+
+- Keep provider seams late-bound during migration: test patching happens after import, while FastAPI dependencies/factory parameters are bound at registration time. Directly capturing `connection`, Mongo getters, simulations, or config values can silently bypass the current tests.
+- Preserve app-state ownership of runtime resources and do not introduce a second pool/client/bus/simulation registry. Do not change route contracts or replace tests with weaker assertions.
+- T331's original ≤120-line target and T332's broad DI scope exceed one small change; continue with one router family per W2 packet, preceded by a W3 test-only fixture or characterization packet.
